I like Qt Nethack, but one really irritating thing about it is how the
message window only saves about the last twenty lines.  When one gets
pounded to death by monsters while helpless, as I have been on
multiple occasions, one can't always tell the reason one became
helpless in the first place.

Today I was in the midst of my most promising Valkyrie run to date (no
ascensions to my name yet).  The only major setback was when I stepped
on a polymorph trap; I just happened to be wearing a ring of polymorph
control and chose "Valkyrie," so I didn't change form, but I lost two
whole levels--damn it!  I still had my original +3 wooden shield, but
it had gotten thoroughly burnt.  I had a scroll of enchant armor and
had been looking for some way to become confused so I could undo the
damage.

Anyway, I reached the castle, and cleared most of it out pretty
effectively, with an AC down around -11.  Some troll or something
threw a potion at me, and I ended up confused.  "Aha!" I thought.
"Just what I've been waiting for!"  Stupidly, I removed all my armor
(including some speed boots) except for the shield, when I noticed
that the confusion had already worn off, and some more monsters had
filed into the throne room and were closing in on me.  "Shit!" I
thought, remembering how I'd recently gotten killed while helpless as
I put on some armor.  I checked my inventory.  There was an athame I'd
just picked up from a lich.  Triumphantly, I engraved Elbereth with
it.  BOOM!  Suddenly I'm dead.

Man, I was so pissed.  I'd been pounded to death by a horde of
monsters while helpess.  But I couldn't tell why!  The reason for my
helplessness had scrolled off the top of the message window.  My only
clue was that the athame was identified as -3 and cursed.  Does that
make a difference?  The Nethack wiki doesn't mention anything about
cursed athames.  If it's not that, all I can think is that some
monster hit me with a potion of paralysis.

Sheesh.  On my road to ascension I'm hitting just about every possible
instadeath.

